^.*symbol 'operator\(\)' is unknown.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
--
Regression for selecting an explicit class-template specialization
whose primary template has a defaulted template parameter
(`template <typename T, typename = void> struct caster;` with
`template <> struct caster<Big>`).  Per [temp.arg]/2 and
[temp.class.spec.match] the specialization's written argument list
<Big> is completed with the primary's default to <Big, void>, matching
a use `caster<Big>` (= caster<Big, void>).  CBMC previously compared
the unequal written sizes and fell back to the empty primary template,
so the specialization's member `operator()` was not found.  This is
the arith_tools `numeric_castt<mp_integer>` / std::optional pattern.
